course: dictionary
lesson: 10285
title: A tort is a wrong, not a cake
level: primary-5
stars: 2
explain: A tort is a law word. It means a wrong done to a person, for example when someone's carelessness hurts you or damages your things. The person harmed can ask a court for money to make things right. Even so, a tort is usually not a crime.
explain: Here is an example. A shop leaves a wet floor with no sign, and a customer slips and falls. The shop was careless, so it committed a tort. This kind of carelessness is called negligence, and negligence is one type of tort. Lawyers talk about «tort law» and «the law of torts» when they study these wrongs.
explain: Context helps you here. Words like «sue», «damages» and «compensation» point to courts and money, not to food. The sentence «tort means a big layered cake» is a mistake. A layered cake is a torte, spelled with an e. Always check the spelling and the clues around a word.
fact: A tort is a wrong done to someone that can lead to a civil court case.
fact: The injured person can sue for damages, which means money, even when the wrong is not a crime.
fact: Negligence, being careless in a way that hurts someone, is one kind of tort.
fact: «Torte» is a rich cake, and «taut» means tight. Neither of them means tort.
exercise: In law, what is a tort? | A kind of pet | A big layered cake for birthdays | *A wrong done to someone that they can take to court for money | A tight rope used by circus workers
exercise: A shop leaves a wet floor with no sign, and a customer slips. Is this a tort? | No, because a tort is always a crime | *Yes, the shop was careless and hurt someone, which is negligence | Yes, because wet floors are always illegal | No, because slipping is never anyone's fault
exercise: A tort is not the same as «torte». What is a torte? | *A rich layered cake | A tight knot | A wrong done to someone | A court case about money
test: Can a tort be taken to a civil court even if it is not a crime? | *Yes, the injured person can sue for damages | No, it is always settled with a cake | No, only crimes can go to court | Yes, but only if a police officer arrests someone
test: What is negligence? | A crime that a judge punishes with prison | A type of cake | *Carelessness that hurts someone, a kind of tort | Keeping things very tight
exam: Which sentence uses tort correctly? | The rope was tort, so it was tight | *The shop's careless wet floor was a tort, and the customer could claim damages | The torte was a wrong done to me | Tort is a big layered cake for birthdays
